{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Ryan, thanks for reaching out. Your account is currently disabled, and the help desk can't re-enable accounts or reset passwords for disabled accounts at Tier 1. Reactivating a returning contractor's account needs confirmation from HR and your manager. I've passed your request to our Tier 2 team, who will contact you. Nothing has been changed on your account yet. Please make sure HR and your sponsoring manager know about your Monday start so the approval can move quickly.",
  "internal_note": "Sender is ryan.brooks (user_id 10), Sales, title 'Account Executive (former)', status DISABLED, not VIP, no lockout. Requests reactivation and password reset as a returning contractor starting Monday. Per KB-005, Tier 1 does not reset, unlock, or re-enable disabled accounts, so no reset_password or unlock_account was requested. Sign-in logs show 2 failed_password attempts on VPN, Sat 2026-10-10 about 03:05-03:07 home time (09:05 Amsterdam), from IP 192.0.2.140 on a hosting network, no MFA, from Amsterdam, NL. Ryan's usual location is America/New_York. This is a possible credential-misuse pattern on a disabled account. Also flag: the account still shows vpn_access=true despite being disabled, which should be checked. Escalated to Tier 2 for security review and for HR/manager verification of the contractor re-engagement. Confirm the requester is Ryan through a callback to the number on file before any re-enable. Do not reset the password until approved.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-005"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
